# Rendered from the YAML on demand. Committing them would create exactly the
# drift between document and suite that generating them prevents.
evals/ask_ai/report.html
evals/ask_ai/investigation.html

# An eval set that is still being written. run_eval.py writes after every run
# so an interruption keeps its evidence, and renames to the real name only
# when the set completes -- but a run started before that change, or a
# `.partial` recovered by hand, still lands here. Committing one turns
# tests/test_documented_measurements.py red with a very convincing "RUNBOOK.md
# says 1973 grounded runs; results/ now has 1985".
results/*.json.partial
results/*.log.partial
